#189-02 one-shot re-selection of past incumbents on a fresh slice (RULES-confirm.md rule 9, amendment ddfaced8) -- w168, 11-14 CST.
Against HEAD 6d0ec11d (driver.py = a677294e's: w167's two-stage accept on top of strata + pool K=3 + cross). Touches
search/v3/driver.py, search/v3/slices.py, search/convplot4.py. CONF "reselect" absent = today's driver event for event
(test_reselect189: on_result replay AND Driver.step replay of the live state, HEAD vs patched; convplot4 output and PNG
byte-identical on the live state of 9:47 PM CST).

Choices the rule leaves open (each pinned by a test in search/v3/confirm189/test_reselect189.py):
 1 Events. "reselect_start" (the plan: per size b, incumbent, candidates {hash, of, tags}), "reselect_size" (ranking rows
   {hash, of, eval, da, z, logr, se, off, k, pass}, verdict switched | kept | error, inc, pool, prev, act), "reselect_done".
   NOT "reselect" per size as the task text said: "reselect" is already RULES-pool §5's per-rotation event and replay sets
   reselected[size] = its slice, so a one-shot event under that name would make a restart (and the old code on a rollback)
   run §5 again on the active slice. The switch's incumbent event carries "why": "reselect9"; pool event why "reselect9".
 2 Candidates per listed size: every "incumbent" tag and every "pool" member at or after state line from_line (inclusive),
   plus the current incumbent and members; deduplicated by MV.ahash(drv/assign/<tag>.json) (a rotation retag is the same
   model; all its tags listed, the first seen is "of"). Models that join before the size is decided are added (rule 9 "plus
   any since"; in confirm mode nothing joins while pending). from_line for the live run = 2 (the only "act" event: a8g128 at
   s173a) -> 89 models at 9:15 PM CST as the rule says, 92 at 9:47 PM.
 3 Evals: kind "reselect", whole slice, no early-stop block, the registry alias; cached per (hash, slice) in the confirm
   cache (cfx; the slices are disjoint by role). A failed eval is resubmitted (CONF reselect.tries, 2); a candidate failing
   twice is listed "failed" and left out; the incumbent's failing twice -> verdict "error", incumbent and pool kept.
   Reselect results are fit rows (labels s186e|...) like confirmation rows; never a decision on the search slice.
 4 Statistic: driver.paired(current incumbent's s186e eval, candidate's) with the slice's strata, CONF cap / guard as in force
   (both null live), offset = the size's b x (bpw_cand - bpw_inc) + decode term; b fixed at the start (recorded, like
   go-live). z = Paired.z() = da / se. Reference = the incumbent when the size's set is complete.
 5 Pick: PR.reseed_pick(incumbent, [(hash, da, z < CONF z)], min(top, K)): ranking by da with the incumbent at 0 (ties to it);
   new incumbent = the best-ranked model with z < -1, else the current one; pool = the top 3 with the new incumbent kept.
   Tags: a model that is a current member keeps its tag (already scored on the active slice); the others get their s186e
   eval tag (assignment written at submit), which ensure_incumbents / ensure_pool rescore whole on the active slice in the
   next step, as at a rotation; no stage-1 decision or tentative of the size is judged before that (scored_on).
   2.0 / 2.5 (pools of 1 since the abandoned re-seed) get pools of up to 3.
 6 RULES-pool §5 (re-selection at a rotation) does not run for a size while its one-shot is pending, and is taken as done on
   the active slice once the one-shot decided the size (reselected[size] = active): the fresh-slice pick stands.
 7 Order: starts in the step rule 7's go-live check completes (CONF confirm.golive_from_line set and no "golive done" =
   wait). A listed size's tentatives wait from the CONF until its "reselect_size" (then rule 3: confirmed against the NEW
   incumbent). Stage-1 decisions and generation go on, but the ~92 queued evals exceed queue_depth (22), so in effect the
   search pauses until the s186e evals drain (~45-60 min at ~120 whole evals / h).
 8 Registry: role "reselect" (slices.py role REG s186e reselect). Registry.ready() skips any slice with a role (confirm,
   reselect); draw_merged treats a reselect slice's calib docs as busy; one "reselect_decisions" count per size (never
   "decisions" / "confirm_decisions"; status stays staged) + doc_decisions. The driver refuses CONF reselect unless the slice
   has the role, was never active (status active / retired or "activated"), never decided or confirmed, is in no confirm
   pair, and from_line is set; the confirm check also refuses a pair slice with role reselect. Pairs a/b, c/d without e/f are
   accepted while s186f keeps role confirm (unused until a new pair is built).
 9 Plot: NO decision event. The s186e log r of the chosen model vs the old incumbent is the best of N measured models on
   the same numbers that pick it (the winner's curse rule 4 avoids), and the old incumbent's chained level already holds
   the pre-#189 stage-1 gains rule 9 doubts; chaining one on the other would not be honest. A decision event would also
   count as a search decision in the driver's replay (dec counts, generation balance) and in offline readers
   (rerank187/replay.py, a8172/a8gap.py). Instead convplot4 treats an incumbent event with why "reselect9" as a LEVEL RESET:
   from that step the size's line is anchored on the new model's own read (--anchor-track: its t183 read; else its monitor
   read; any tag with the same assignment hash), with later accepts chained on it; with no read yet the level is held and
   the footnote names the size. Without such events convplot4's output is unchanged.
10 Rollback: the old code ignores reselect_* events; incumbent / pool / submit events are standard, so its replay lands on
   the same incumbents and pools; it may run §5 once on the active slice for re-selected sizes (item 6 is not in its state).
Not handled: go-live reverts are incumbent changes without a decision too, and convplot4 keeps the reverted accepts' chained
log r (live: 3.0-5.0 reverted 9:40-9:44 PM CST; the b2 line stayed 0.598). Passing why="golive" in golive_step's
set_incumbent and accepting it in convplot4's reset test would give them the same level reset: the lead's call.

